public import Mathlib

/-!
# Khintchine inequality and empirical sampling

This file was automatically generated by Codex.

The Khintchine upper moment inequality for finite sums in real or complex
inner product spaces, two independent sign randomizations, and the empirical
sampling estimate for complex functions on arbitrary finite abelian groups.
For exponent p at least two and n positive independent uniform samples, the
expected pth power of the normalized Lp sampling error is at most
(4 sqrt(p/n) times the Lp norm of the function) to the pth power.
All statements and supporting definitions use only Mathlib and this module.
The sampling theorem is extended to the Croot-Sisask almost-period argument
using Markov's inequality, diagonal tuple fibers and translation invariance.
Probability-normalized Fourier inversion and Parseval give the general
trilinear correlation extraction estimate used by the finite inverse theorem.

Verified source: blueprint/formalization_blueprint.tex, lem:finite-fourier,
lines 177-209. The proof uses independent-copy symmetrization, the Khintchine
inequality and finite probability-space norm inequalities. The upper-moment
proof is adapted from ../lean-variationalsw as attributed below.
-/

@[expose] public section

section

namespace Auto
open Filter Polynomial MeasureTheory
open scoped Topology BigOperators ENNReal ComplexConjugate

/-- Probability-counting expectation written as a finite sum. -/
noncomputable def finiteAverage {G : Type*} [Fintype G] (f : G → ℂ) : ℂ :=
  (Fintype.card G : ℂ)⁻¹ * ∑ x, f x

                                                                                    
                                                                        
                                                                         

